# Docker build context, for `server/Dockerfile`.
#
# The context is the repository ROOT, because the relay's source imports
# `../../shared/signaling-protocol`. That means the studio's whole tree is in
# scope by default, so most of this file is about keeping it out — a smaller
# context is a faster upload and a better layer cache.
#
# `shared/` and `server/` are the two directories that must NOT be excluded.

# ----------------------------------------------------------- never ship these
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# Build output. The image builds its own from source; copying a host build in
# would produce an image whose contents depend on whoever ran docker build.
dist
server/dist
server/.next
.next

# Local environment. Secrets and ports belong in the host's configuration, not
# baked into a layer where anyone who can pull the image can read them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --------------------------------------------- the studio, which is not the relay
# The browser client is deployed as static files elsewhere; the relay needs
# none of it. `shared/` is the only code the two have in common.
src
e2e
public
index.html
vite.config.ts
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.app.json
tsconfig.node.json
.oxlintrc.json
package.json
package-lock.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------- test artefacts
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright/.cache
coverage

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ editor/local
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
README.md
